From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: artzig <artzig@localhost>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 23:12:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DevicePolicyManager: cut unavailable host backends

The hosted system exposes the stock device-policy client over a deliberately
empty IDevicePolicyManager implementation. It has no Android zygote or ARM MTE,
NFC stack, VPN-aware kernel traffic accounting, or Soong jarjar packaging.

Keep the stock client surface and private-DNS TLS probe while cutting those
unavailable implementation edges. NFC provisioning reports no result, MTE is
not enforced on the x86_64 host, and the nano runtime uses its direct AOSP
namespace.

The platform build also jarjars modules-utils' string list parcelable into
android.content.pm. Direct javac retains its source namespace, so use that
equivalent type in the two internal AIDL declarations.

